      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228528/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine water, elderberries, ginger, cinnamon stick, and cloves in a saucepan over medium heat; bring to a boil. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ceEHTZcvNLoBRd-mA1vXg-LseNo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-228528-elderberry-syrup-DDMFS-Step-2-fb2f37cdfbab412492754a24cb5aed89.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228528/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mash berries with a potato mixture to release juices.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/1YnFiM5gaQLiHHDQJA69OvsoaYc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-228528-elderberry-syrup-DDMFS-Step-3-1891879ebc9a43a995aaf87481a85dac.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/228528/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strain the mixture through a fine sieve, retaining juice and discarding pulp, cinnamon stick, and cloves. Let cool for 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
